<article class="env-remark" id="0G1Y">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0G1Y">Remark <span data-tag="0G1Y">19.13.9</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{A}$ be a Grothendieck abelian category. Let $M, K$ be objects of $D(\mathcal{A})$. For any choice of complex $K^\bullet $ representing $K$ we can use the filtration $F^ pK^\bullet = \tau _{\leq -p}K^\bullet $ and the discussion in Remark <a href="/tag/0G1X" data-tag="0G1X">19.13.8</a> to get a spectral sequence with </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  E_1^{p, q} = \mathop{\mathrm{Ext}}\nolimits ^{2p + q}(M, H^{-p}(K))  \]
</div>
  <p> This spectral sequence is independent of the choice of complex $K^\bullet $ representing $K$. After renumbering $p = -j$ and $q = i + 2j$ we find a spectral sequence $(E'_ r, d'_ r)_{r \geq 2}$ with $d'_ r$ of bidegree $(r, -r + 1)$, with </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  (E'_2)^{i, j} = \mathop{\mathrm{Ext}}\nolimits ^ i(M, H^ j(K))  \]
</div>
  <p> If $M \in D^-(\mathcal{A})$ and $K \in D^+(\mathcal{A})$ then both $E_ r$ and $E'_ r$ are bounded and converge to $\mathop{\mathrm{Ext}}\nolimits ^{p + q}(M, K)$. If we use the filtration $F^ pK^\bullet = \sigma _{\geq p}K^\bullet $ then we get </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  E_1^{p, q} = \mathop{\mathrm{Ext}}\nolimits ^ q(M, K^ p)  \]
</div>
  <p> If $M \in D^-(\mathcal{A})$ and $K^\bullet $ is bounded below, then this spectral sequence is bounded and converges to $\mathop{\mathrm{Ext}}\nolimits ^{p + q}(M, K)$. </p>
</article>